WEBVTT

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.980
Why did you do that?!

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.140
No particular reason.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.630
I just made the most effective use 
of someone not especially useful.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.790
There's no way you can get away with that!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.080
The last one standing takes everything.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.540
There are no rules.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:28.000
This is an exceedingly simple competition.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.270
You're free to participate, or to quit.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.010
Only one thing is demanded of you:

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:36.540
The resolve to throw away everything

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.780
in order to make your wish come true.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.330
Hey, Four-eyes.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.750
Why are you looking for the Collection?

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.230
Because...

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.360
That's your true nature.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.020
If you just want to play buddy-buddy,

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.240
then quit now, like all the others did.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.580
Of course, even if you don't quit, I will.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.530
The moment Kasumi left,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.030
this club lost any value it had.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.330
Konjou-senpai...

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:46.970
Are you going somewhere?

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:52.800
<b><u>Episode 9</u></b>

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:52.800
A Study of Ikusaba Hiiyo and Yoshino Saki

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:49.740
Yeah. Southred Mall.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.460
You're really going all-out.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.230
I've got a date today.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.110
With Yukihime-neesan again?

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.860
No, the class president with the glasses.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.820
Are you really that popular?

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.990
Is it really a date?

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.400
I'm sorry. I lied.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.030
We're actually going to hang 
out with a new guy in our class

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:13.640
and another friend I met recently.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:14.920
You were so obvious.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.900
<i>Good morning, Satsumi-kun!</i>

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.400
Tensai-chan and Daruku-chan 
aren't going with you?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.410
<b>Good morning. Wanna walk to school together? 

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:19.380
<i>O-Okay...</i>

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.520
They still haven't come 
back to their room today.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.500
I see...

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.530
Yet, you went to check on them.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.210
You're worried, aren't you?

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.230
I'm not! I just happened to be there!

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.810
Yumeji-san!

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.830
Hello.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:41.700
Hello!

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.020
Your outfit looks really nice.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.680
You're prettier than ever today!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.390
I-I'm not...

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.410
You look... very nice, too.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.870
Good morning!

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:57.960
Yama-senpai!

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.630
Thanks for inviting me along today!

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.980
That was such a good movie!

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:16.980
It didn't scare you?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.410
It didn't scare me at all!

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.200
Besides, I could've gotten 
away from that crazy killer!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.330
Yeah, I bet you could, Yun.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.620
Did you handle it okay, Yumeji-san?

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.390
It was scary, but I enjoyed it.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.260
Oh, there's something in your hair.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.300
Hm? Where?

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.340
Not there. A little higher...

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.950
Just some lint...

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.250
<i>I know I just sensed a murderous aura...</i>

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.530
U-Um, Yama-kun...

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:00.530
Oh, um... I didn't...

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.030
This is not the time nor place,
 Yama Juugo!

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:06.990
I can't see! I can't see anything!

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:12.840
<i>Who do you like more, me or her?</i>

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.910
<b>You, of course. 

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.910
What a mess.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:23.770
Sexy.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.310
Who sent you?

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.280
I don't intend to answer that.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.790
Is that so?

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:45.940
Then die.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.590
Show a little more spirit 
when you run from me.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.420
<i>He kept up with my movements?</i>

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.050
Done already?

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.840
<i>He got ahead of me?!</i>

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:14.520
Sorry.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.990
This place is like my backyard.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:20.220
You're certainly quick...

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.190
Your agility is quite a nuisance.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:25.650
Be careful.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.840
Your right leg is going to go numb,

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.450
then you'll lose your balance and fall.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.550
You can't get back up.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:36.450
<i>I can't move!</i>

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:37.910
<i>What happened?!</i>

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.850
<i>That man, Ikusaba Hiiyo,</i>

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:44.260
<i>was the most proficient
 of all the original members</i>

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.310
<i>in the use of Nanana's Collection.</i>

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:46.510
Bye, now.

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:51.030
Thanks for today!

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.300
See you at school tomorrow.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:53.990
Goodbye.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:54.930
See ya.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.570
Bye! Remember to go straight home!

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.010
Let me walk you back to your dorm.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.350
You don't have to worry about me.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.030
Okay...

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.410
Yep! Goodnight!

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.000
I'm home.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.460
Welcome back!

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:28.030
Hurry up!

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:28.780
Huh?

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.070
The Japanese-style brown sugar

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.510
syrup pudding from
 Tenjikudo in Southred Mall!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.990
It's sweet, but not too 
sweet, and so elegant.

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.450
It's one of the highest
 puddings in my personal ranking!

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.520
Juugo?

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.850
Sorry.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:53.360
I was so preoccupied with playing 
around, that didn't even occur to me.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.240
You'll pay.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.040
Hey... What are you...

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:02.770
Stop!

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:08.710
Why a Palo Special?!

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:12.170
Hey. Long time no see.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:17.090
All traces of you disappeared 
since then, so I had given up...

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.400
I never imagined I'd see you again like this.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.560
Wh-What do you mean?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.290
How did you get out?

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.900
I've verified that you didn't clear it.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:28.980
Where were you all this time?

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.340
I-I have no idea
 what you're talking about...

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:35.610
Why don't you drop
 that ridiculous act already?

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.830
Wait. You know me, don't you?

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:45.910
Y-You said at the arcade
 that your name is Ikusaba-san.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:47.330
No, I didn't mean...

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.530
What is going on here?

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.090
Hold it. We're not done talking.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.470
Answer my question.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.430
<i>Help! Help!</i>

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.180
<i>Tetsu!</i>

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:06.030
<i>Yun, are you all right?</i>

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:08.700
Hey there, boyfriend-kun.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:12.820
Stalking your girlfriend 
is just short of criminal.

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.280
Better than being a real stalker.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.740
Is that real?

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:24.000
There are only so many people 
on this island with real swords.

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:27.200
Are you from the Tsukuyomi District?

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:28.460
What if I am?

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.210
You're not one of the Three Skulls, are you?

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:37.680
This sucks. I had no idea 
Kurosu Sansa was involved.

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.430
You're going to tell me everything you know!

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.060
Looks like I can't do 
anything against a blade.

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:47.270
Then make this easy and start talking!

00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:48.670
I refuse.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.270
Let's go.

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:01.830
Too bad.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:25.390
What's wrong? Come at me.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:33.540
You're like a samurai who's 
behind the times, boyfriend-kun.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.030
Over here, officer!

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.400
There's a bad guy over here!

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.820
Sorry, but I'm leaving.

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:48.060
Do that.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.230
I don't want to deal with cops, either.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.100
Are you okay, Tetsu?

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.590
Yeah. What about you, Yun?

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:59.090
Yeah. You came for me, so I'm fine.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:00.700
Where are the police?

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.050
Oh, that was a lie.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:06.000
I thought he would go away if I did that.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.060
I see...

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:10.870
Anyway, we need to contact Sister.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:16.280
Huh? Why would Ikusaba-san attack Yun-chan?

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.600
I don't know.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.580
Yama Juugo,

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:21.770
I have a favor to ask you.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:22.930
A favor?

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:26.740
I want you to make sure Ikusaba 
Hiiyo never goes near Yun again.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.140
Huh? Why me?

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:32.660
Honestly, I'd love to take the 
initiative and slice him apart,

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:36.210
but I need to focus on 
protecting Yun this time.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.500
You object?

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:41.420
Not at all.
 In fact, I'd be glad to do it.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:44.930
It's for Yun-chan, and if it's 
a favor to you, all the better.

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.630
So I want you to tell me the truth.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:50.940
Right...

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:55.730
Juugo, I must apologize to you.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.130
It's true that asking
 this of you wasn't my idea.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.200
I thought so.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:05.530
Sister told me to have Yama 
Juugo do something about it.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:06.510
She named me?!

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.680
I don't know why Sister
 told me to ask this of you...

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:13.660
But Ikusaba is strong.

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.380
There's only so much I can do on my own.

00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:20.430
Please, Juugo.

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.800
Sure! Leave getting rid of Ikusaba-san to me!

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.620
Hello.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.250
Ah, Yama-kun.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:31.340
Tsurezure-senpai! What happened to you?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.190
Don't ask about it.

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.060
Okay.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:37.050
There's something I'd like to ask you all.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:39.400
What're you being so formal for?

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:42.320
Do you know someone named Ikusaba Hiiyo?

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.270
Huh?

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:48.240
What does that reaction mean?

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:51.790
I see...

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.990
Ikusaba-san attended
 this school until last year,

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:59.040
and he seemed to know 
about Nanana's Collection,

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:02.260
so I thought you all might know something.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.930
Your deduction was correct.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:10.250
Ikusaba Hiiyo was vice president
 of the original Adventure Club

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:11.970
and the second president.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:15.310
He's also the man who once 
crushed the Adventure Club.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:19.700
The founder of the Adventure Club

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:22.540
was its first president, Konjou Kasumi-senpai.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.870
Under Konjou-senpai,
 the Third High School Adventure Club

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.690
had fun while steadily acquiring
 the treasures of Nanana's Collection.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.830
But then the end came.

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.280
When Konjou-senpai graduated,

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.420
she left the Adventure Club and Nanae Island.

00:13:42.390 --> 00:13:46.290
It was Ikusaba-san who
 took over the club after her.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.820
But Ikusaba-san was a man

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.760
who had no qualms about
 using very forceful methods.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:57.230
Club Resignation

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:57.230
So the members at the
 time quit the club, one by one.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.690
And then... something worse happened.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:07.110
Ikusaba-san sacrificed one of 
his club members in the ruins.

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.710
We did obtain the
 Nanana's Collection treasure,

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:20.170
but...

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.060
"I shouldn't have joined this club."

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:27.430
That's what she said to 
me as she left the island.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.430
Then Ikusaba-san took the

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.410
Nanana's Collection treasure 
we'd found, and quit the club.

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:36.620
In the end, only I remained,

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.560
but I was essentially a ghost member.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:40.980
I might as well have quit.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:43.440
Then, what about the current club?

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:48.140
I invited Yuu and Kagetora to join 
me and reopened the club this spring,

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:49.590
as its third president.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:52.830
Ikusaba-san came here not long ago, as well.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.380
You mean...

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:58.520
Yes. He probably came to find 
information on Yoshino Saki-san.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:01.760
Yama-kun,

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:05.030
if you're looking to pick 
a fight with Ikusaba-san,

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:07.890
I know we can't do much,
 but I want you to let us help.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.340
Please do.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:15.480
The first question is, why did 
Ikusaba-san attack Yoshino-san?

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.770
I can answer that.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:24.270
Tensai! Where have you been?!

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.480
Long time no see, Juugo.
 As a matter of fact,

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:32.230
I accepted a secret job offer
 from a first-year named Suruga Aya.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:33.220
That job entailed...

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.490
W-Wait a minute!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.700
Where were you, and what were you doing?!

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:40.610
We've been looking into
 something for the past few days.

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:41.560
Huh?!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.160
Let's hear her out.

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:47.000
The secret job offer I accepted

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.280
was to search for a student 
who went missing a month ago.

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:51.680
But...

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:55.050
The girl turned up
 before I could bring her back!

00:15:55.750 --> 00:15:58.930
But what does that have to do with Yun-chan?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.670
The missing student was Yoshino Saki.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.190
And why are you so angry?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.440
What are you saying?!

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:14.040
The case solved itself 
before I got to do anything!

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:18.000
Frankly, it's humiliating! You can only
 suffer such insults for so long!

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.040
My pride as a master
 detective will not let this slide!

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:24.050
That's why Tensai continued investigating

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:26.900
after the girl returned,
 to find out what really happened.

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:29.250
I have a question for you, Yuiga-dono.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.220
I want to know about the 
man called Ikusaba Hiiyo.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:38.930
On the day Yoshino Saki went missing, 
she was doing something.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:41.370
It was a secret job.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:43.930
It entailed investigating a certain building.

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.400
The one offering the job was...

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:47.400
Ikusaba-san?

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:50.280
Yes. Ikusaba Hiiyo.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.530
And the "building" most likely referred to ruins.

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:56.180
Wait a second!

00:16:56.180 --> 00:17:00.100
You're saying Yun-chan knows
 about ruins and Nanana's Collection?

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:03.750
No, I believe Yoshino-san was probably used.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:05.520
So she just took the job

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:09.460
for the money, knowing nothing, 
and carried it out?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.150
Probably.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:13.290
Using someone like that
 and then discarding them

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:15.720
is the sort of thing Ikusaba-san does.

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:19.480
So you think this Yoshino is being targeted

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:23.180
because she found out 
something about the ruins?

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.480
That's very possible.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.320
But let's say Yoshino Saki did
 find out something about the ruins.

00:17:29.530 --> 00:17:32.030
Where was she and what
 was she doing during

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.110
during the time she was considered missing?

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:39.250
Um, I just happened to find this
 out while I was doing a secret job...

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.910
Until recently, Yun-chan was part of

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.410
a scary-looking group
 in the Tsukuyomi District.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.800
Was it the group in charge
 of that area, the Three Skulls?

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:49.530
So you think the first-year called Yoshino Saki

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:52.940
returned because she
 had that group's backing?

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.750
Not bad.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:59.500
No, I can't imagine
 Yun-chan using them like that.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.590
Also, it looked like she had never met

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:03.180
Ikusaba-san before at the arcade.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.670
Are you sure it wasn't your imagination?

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:08.020
No, it didn't seem that way.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.990
Anyway, now that we know this much,

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:11.690
it's clear what we need to do.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:13.940
What's that?

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.430
Yoshino-san is being targeted

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.870
because she has information about the ruins.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.450
So if we clear those ruins first...

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:26.900
Ikusaba-san will have no
 more reason to target Yun-chan.

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:29.370
Then, let's ask Yun-chan!

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:32.020
No. We don't want Ikusaba-san to realize

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:36.420
we're in contact with her and
 find out we're after the same ruins.

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:37.380
He's right.

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:41.390
We don't know how he's watching this girl.

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:43.640
Where's the ruins?

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:46.890
I know it's in Southred Mall.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.670
That's where?

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.650
How do we search a huge place like that?

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:54.110
We'll just have to go and get a hint, then.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.490
A hint? I can't.

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:58.450
Just this once?

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.730
Nope. Not telling.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.290
Nanana-chan, please!

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:03.380
No.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.630
I'm begging you!

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:07.770
You already know the
 location of the ruins, don't you?

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:11.040
So why can't you take 
your time looking for it?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.410
We can't waste time!

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:14.640
Why?

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:16.970
I can't explain this in detail,

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.170
but if we don't clear it soon,
 there'll be trouble!

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.430
Why can't you tell me your reason?

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.850
I can't say.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:31.600
You want me to give you a hint, 
and you won't even tell me why?

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.220
Sorry! But seriously, I'm begging you!

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:37.440
We need to clear these 
ruins as soon as possible!

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:41.320
Please! I'll do anything!

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.020
Give me a hint!

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.370
You just need to clear it?

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:49.200
Yeah!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.960
Okay. I'll tell you.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.290
You will?!

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.460
But I have one condition.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:00.590
Tenjikudo's brown sugar syrup pudding?

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.240
But I have two conditions.

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:08.670
If you do acquire the treasure from the ruins,

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:11.320
you are never to use it.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:13.800
That's my condition.

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:15.020
I can't use it?

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:19.310
Right. No matter what its power is,

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:21.390
you must never use it.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:22.920
You can promise that, right?

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:25.780
You said you only need to clear it, after all.

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:30.200
Okay. I promise.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.040
Goodnight.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:34.880
Goodnight.

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:41.550
<i>What does she mean, I can't use it?</i>

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:46.470
<i>It might be something that
 can help me find her killer...</i>

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:52.420
<i>Does she not want me to find the killer?</i>

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.630
<i>She doesn't want me to find the killer?</i>

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:01.570
<i>She doesn't want to pass on?</i>

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.650
<i>What is it she really wants?</i>
